#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# bilateral_hypergeometric_pfq

#% text
# `bilateral_hypergeometric_pfq([a1, ..., ap], [b1, ..., bq], z)` gives the bilateral hypergeometric series, the sum over all integers `n` of `prod (a_i)_n/prod (b_j)_n z^n`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# With `(a)_(-n) = (-1)^n/(1 - a)_n` the sum is `(p+1)F(q)([a, 1], [b], z) + (q+1)F(p)([1 - b, 1], [1 - a], (-1)^(p - q)/z) - 1`; for `p = q` one of the two series lies outside its disk and is continued by DLMF 16.8.8.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values; `z = 0` gives 0.

#% item
# Lists of `z` thread.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
bilateral_hypergeometric_pfq([1/2, 3/4], [1/4, -1/3], 5.4)
#% output
#= 1.1824894397340397 + 3.0380243014176918im

#% cell
n(bilateral_hypergeometric_pfq([1/2, 3/4], [1/4, 1/3], 5), 30)
#% output
#= 2.31258794352563689208441175328473 + 1.26104601150556993682620420807917im

#% cell
bilateral_hypergeometric_pfq([1/2, 3/4], [1/4, 1/3], [0.1, 0.3, 0.5])
#% output
#= [1.045820881982964 + 0.42629421764716163im, 3.8934650653815055 + 1.8794036378369892im, 10.346160813725444 + 5.243267854258829im]

#% cell
bilateral_hypergeometric_pfq([a1, a2], [b1, b2], 0)
#% output
#= 0

